"hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:"
1116,"Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman Al-Muradi and Nasr bin Marzuq narrated to us strange news. They said: Asad bin Musa narrated to us. Al-Layth bin Saad narrated to us. Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, Qays bin Amr, “He prayed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the morning, and he did not kneel The two rak'ahs of Fajr, and when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, greeted him, he stood up and performed the two rak'ahs of Fajr, while the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was watching. To him, but he did not deny it.” Abu Al-Hasan Omar bin Hafs told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Saad bin Saeed, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim. On the authority of Qays Saad’s grandfather, he prayed with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the morning, then he stood up and prayed two rak’ahs, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “What These two rak'ahs? He said: O Messenger of God, there are two dawn rak'ahs that I had not prayed before, so they are like this. He said: ""Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, remained silent about him."""
